<title>USA: BPA offers 200 MW firm, peak power for Thursday.</title>
<headline>BPA offers 200 MW firm, peak power for Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) said it has 200 megawatts (MW) of firm, peak electricity to sell for Thursday after offering no energy for delivery today.</p>
<p>The federal agency offered to sell surplus firm power for Thursday at $35.00 a megawatt hour (MWh) for Northwest delivery and $42.00 a MWh for California-Oregon border (COB) delivery.</p>
<p>On Monday, BPA offered day-ahead firm, peak energy at $25.00 per MWh for Northwest sales and $26.00 for COB sales.</p>
<p>The agency also offered only 200 MW for Tuesday sales.</p>
<p>((--R Leong, New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
</text>
